Z||000007||loafer87gt||10-29-2001||12:57 PM||||Spiders don't bother me, but man do I hate moths. When I was little kid my parents were doing renovations to our farm house and the ceiling of my room hadn't been finished with drywall yet. I can remember looking up while I was trying to go to sleep and watching the moths move around behind the clear plastic sheeting covering the insulation on the ceiling. Used to creep me out.||||reg||1
Z||000008||JSocha||10-29-2001||01:16 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  I hate spiders...even the little itty, bitty, bitty ones.<P>Severe case of aracnaphobia here.  <P>My kids use this to terrorize me all the time.  They think its absolutely hillarious to point out the miniture decendents of tarantuals.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Its all fun and games now.  <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"> But watch...one day, I will start clutching at my left arm, gasping for air and collapsing from a massive coranary.  Then see who eventually has terrorized who!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||8
Z||000009||fogglethorpe||10-29-2001||05:08 PM||||Eeeeeeeeeeek! Spiders...I hate them. Whenever I see one, I imagine it spinning a sticky web for a fly, then sadistically stalking it before finally pouncing on it and eating its head! Oooooh, the crunching noises are enough to make me ill! Arrrrrgh!<P>..............<BR>&lt;runs quickly to bathroom&gt;||||reg||1
Z||000010||GarethWright||10-29-2001||06:09 PM||||I don't mind bugs, as long as they aren't in the same house or room or car as me, if they are, they DIE!  <BR>Once I was going to stop reading my book and go to sleep, but decided against it, about 3 mins later a HUGE (like almost 1/2 inch across) spider crawled up onto my pillow.  Needless to say, It didn't last long.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Raydar||10-29-2001||09:12 PM||||I got bitten by a (I think) Brown Recluse spider, about 10 years ago. Never even saw the little bastard. That's just what they thought it was. Spent three days in the hospital being pumped full of antibiotics and steroids. Was *not* fun. I'll spare you all the gory details.<BR>I've heard horror stories about Brown Recluse bites. Supposed to leave nasty wounds. But thanks to all the drugs (I suppose) and the early treatment, it never even left a scar. They called me Spider Man at work, for a while.<P>Spiders are fascinating to me, though. There used to be a big Writing Spider outside my old house. Sucker was 2 inches across. Wove a web three <I>feet</I> across, with all sorts of interesting zigzag patterns. He was there for over a month, until a storm blew him down.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Some mornings, it just isn't worth chewing through the restraints.</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 10-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||WampusCat||10-29-2001||09:50 PM||||When I lived in AZ, at certain times of the year the tarantulas would migrate or something.  You could drive out into the desert at night and shine a light and you would see thousands of big hairy tarantulas all walking in the same direction.  Creepy.<BR>  My favorite desert bug was the vinegaroon.  It's kind of like a scorpion, only uglier.<p>[This message has been edited by WampusCat (edited 10-29-2001).]||||reg||1
