Z||000015||Hippocrat||10-29-2001||11:25 PM||||Don't worry about it too much. <P>I would not, did not, teach or permit my son to learn or sing "the itsy bitsy spider".  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>And they say that rock music is just about the shock value. What about that twisted little tale of fear.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><P> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Cooter||10-29-2001||11:29 PM||||A while back, I stepped to the outhouse at the shop to take care of business and saw what I thought was a joke. It was a shiny black plastic spider right by the door. Everyone knows that I hate/fear/hate spiders, so I thought "Y'all are going to have to do better than that to scare me." I reached down to pick up the plastic spider when it jumped toward my hand! It turns out that black widow spiders look like black shiny plastic. I about jumped out of my skin! Needles to say, it got a nice bath of lacquer thinner  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000017||onfire||10-30-2001||06:07 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Philphine:<BR><B><BR>STOP LAUGHING. IT'S NOT FUNNY!!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey. How did you know I was laughing? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"><P>Actually I can't stand anything with more than four legs.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/onfiresigtoo.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000018||LZeitgeist||10-30-2001||08:24 AM||||&lt;bleaugh&gt; ::shudder::<P>I *hate* spiders. I <B>abhor</B> the sneaky, conniving little b*stards. <P>They only make me jump if they're unexpectedly in (or close to) my 'personal space'. Once I get out of range, I stalk and hunt the little b*stard down and kill it. <P>When I kill it, I make *damn* sure it's dead. I want to see a corpse. Or at least a smear. I don't just push the couch against the wall and hope I squashed it... I *move* the couch and find it and then kill it good, where it ain't coming back. <P>I know that if I see one, and I let it live, it will snicker at my stupidity and drop down the back of my shirt the next chance it gets. Or it will wait under my bed until the lights go out, and then it will have its wicked way with me, all over my unconscious face. Evil, nasty, mean little b*stards. <P>Arrgh... ::shudder::  &lt;bleah&gt;||||reg||1
Z||000019||ChopTop||10-30-2001||09:16 AM||||Hehehe, sounds like you guys are perfect customers for the new movie that's named what else...SPIDERS!!!  I saw 13 Ghosts this past weekend and they showed a promo for the movie, some of the spiders were as big as houses.  ||||reg||1
Z||000020||LZeitgeist||10-30-2001||10:00 AM||||If I was forced to see a spider movie in a theatre, you would consider yourself fortunate not to sit within whacking range of me... I'd be slapping at any stray current of air that brushed past me, and anything else that got in the way... LOL!||||reg||1
Z||000021||Raydar||10-30-2001||11:43 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Philphine:<BR><B> <BR>ok. i'm at work now and will be going home to bed in a few hours. you're not helping    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif">   .</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Okay. That was ten years ago. I'm 44 years old and have bitten by a spider exactly *once*. <BR>Chances are, if you saw a spider, it was not a brown recluse. They like to hide, and will usually only bite if you disturb them in their hiding places.<BR>Also, Black Widows like to spin webs in out-of-the-way places and just wait for something to come along and get trapped. <BR>What I'm getting at, is that the poisonous spiders like to hide. <BR>They are <I>not</I> gonna come after you and bite you.  <P>I see spiders in/around my house once in a while. Just brown Wood spiders. They are harmless. Usually run like hell as soon as they see you. <P>Also, I used to know a girl who worked in the pet department at Zayre. (Kinda like K-Mart, years ago.) She used to <I>pet</I> the tarantulas in the pet dept. <BR>As big and ugly as they are, they're not poisonous. Ive heard that a tarantula bite is like a bee sting, at worst. <P><BR>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Some mornings, it just isn't worth chewing through the restraints.</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 10-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||Jaygee79||10-30-2001||12:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fogglethorpe:<BR><B>Eeeeeeeeeeek! Spiders...I hate them. Whenever I see one, I imagine it spinning a sticky web for a fly, then sadistically stalking it before finally pouncing on it and eating its head! Oooooh, the crunching noises are enough to make me ill! Arrrrrgh!<P>..............<BR>&lt;runs quickly to bathroom&gt;</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>well I <B>WAS</B> eating a piece of cucumber when I read this.  Thanks foggle, my salad just wont be the same now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
