Z||000027||GarethWright||10-30-2001||03:35 PM||||Aww aint that cute? <BR>I know I said I kill spiders on sight, but if I know what type they are, sometimes they are Ok<BR>Right now I have a problem with little sand colored ones, because during the night they leave web strands ALL OVER my car.  I used to have a Ford Falcon, that had a spider living in it, about 1/4 inch across, Dark black, Bright green eyes, and Hairy.  I couldnt catch it to kill it so I looked it up in my spider book, turns out it was a kind of spider that Eats Tons of bugs every night, so I let it live.<BR>Also, while my Mom was gardening she found a spider that was glossy black with a red design on its back, I was all for squishing it, but she said "no, its not doing anything, leave it alone" so I once again pulled out the handy spider book, found that is WAS a Black Widow, read to her what happens when a BW bites you, then proceeded to Hose it with wasp killer.  It swam happily around in the puddle I made for a while, so I used the ole Mark I spider killer, and stomped on it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
